+{% comment %}
+   D-08: event.telescope_label_meta is CalendarEventMeta's reverse one-to-one accessor
+   (related_name, unchanged by the Phase 27 rename). A reverse one-to-one miss raises
+   ObjectDoesNotExist, which Django templates swallow (silent_variable_failure) -- the same
+   mechanism calendar.html's own is_verified branches already rely on -- so a conference,
+   proposal deadline, or any other event with no companion row at all renders exactly as it
+   does today, with no run block.
+
+   WR-03 (27-07 gap closure, 27-UAT.md Test 9): Phase 29's reconciler
+   (campaign_reconciler.py's reconcile_run(), both the container and classical-nights
+   branches) now writes CalendarEventMeta.run automatically for every event it creates or
+   adopts, unconditionally, via _link_event_to_run(). An event from a pipeline the
+   reconciler doesn't own -- raw sync_lco_observation_calendar/sync_gemini_observation_calendar/
+   load_telescope_runs output not yet adopted by any run -- still has no link until a staff
+   member hand-links it via the admin CalendarEventMetaInline picker or confirms a match in
+   the Phase 28 attribution queue. The block added below now surfaces a HIGH-band
+   attribution-queue candidate for exactly that still-unlinked case, so the modal is never
+   silently empty when a good match already exists. See
+   docs/runbooks/telescope_runs_calendar.rst, "Why doesn't the calendar pop-up show a
+   'Campaign run' block?".
+{% endcomment %}
+{% comment %}
+   D-14/D-17 (Phase 33): CalendarEventMeta.run means the event is ATTRIBUTED to that
+   run, never that the run OWNS it. The block below is rendered from that link at
+   request time via campaign_decoration() -- nothing is written to the event's own
+   fields -- so a base-layer re-projection of this event's title/description cannot
+   erase the attribution.
+   WR-07 (Phase 33 Plan 06): campaign_decoration()'s own `run is None or not
+   run.is_publicly_visible` rule is now the ONLY place that visibility gate lives --
+   there is no second, independent `run.is_publicly_visible` gate in this template.
+   A run not yet approved therefore renders no link here, for every user including
+   staff -- mirrors CampaignRunTableView.get_queryset()'s existing exclude(). There is
+   no run-detail view today (D-06 defers it to Phase 28, where the attribution UI it
+   would host gets built), so the run's identity is rendered inline here rather than
+   relying on the link alone to answer "which run is this" -- and the link below
+   targets the campaign table instead. Contact fields and source are deliberately
+   never rendered here: this modal is a non-staff-visible surface, contact fields are
+   PII gated elsewhere by contact_public_opt_in, and source is staff-only per D-18.
+   A reverse one-to-one accessor with no row (event.telescope_label_meta) resolves
+   silently in a template because ObjectDoesNotExist sets silent_variable_failure --
+   campaign_decoration() itself guards this, so no {% with %} wrapper is needed here
+   to pre-resolve it.
+{% endcomment %}
+{% comment %}
+   PROJ-04/PROJ-05 (Phase 34 Plan 03, D-04): series identity is read from the companion
+   row's observation_group link at request time via observation_series_decoration() --
+   nothing is written into the event's own title or description -- so a re-projection of
+   this event cannot erase it. This block is a sibling of the campaign-decoration block
+   above, not nested inside it: a record can be in a group with no campaign, or attributed
+   to a campaign with no group, and both cases must render independently.
+{% endcomment %}
+{% observation_series_decoration event as series %}
+{% if series %}
+    <div class="row">
+      <div class="col">
+        <label>Observation series</label>
+        <div>
+          <a href="{{ series.group_list_url }}" target="_blank">{{ series.group_name }} ↗</a>
+          &mdash; Night {{ series.index }} of {{ series.size }}
+          &mdash; <a href="{{ series.record_url }}" target="_blank">View record ↗</a>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+    </div>
+{% endif %}
+{% campaign_decoration event as deco %}
+{% if deco %}
+    <div class="row">
+      <div class="col">
+        <label>
+          Attributed campaign run
+          <small>
+            {% if deco.table_url %}
+            <a href="{{ deco.table_url }}" target="_blank">View campaign ↗</a>
+            {% endif %}
+          </small>
+        </label>
+        <div>
+          {{ deco.campaign_name }} &mdash; {{ deco.telescope_instrument }}
+          {% comment %}
+             WR-04: window_start and window_end are guaranteed both-NULL or both-set by
+             the campaign_run_window_start_end_null_together CheckConstraint, so gating
+             on window_start alone is sufficient -- a TBD run (both NULL) must not render
+             the literal "(None-None)" here.
+          {% endcomment %}
+          {% if deco.window_start %}
+          ({{ deco.window_start }}&ndash;{{ deco.window_end }})
+          {% endif %}
+          &mdash; {{ deco.run_status_display }}
+        </div>
+        {% comment %}
+           D-09/TALLY-01 (Phase 37 Plan 06): the run's live tally, read from the same
+           run.is_publicly_visible-gated link campaign_decoration() already applied above --
+           deliberately rendered INSIDE this {% if deco %} block, not behind a second
+           top-level {% if %}, so the visibility gate is applied once. run_tally() mirrors
+           campaign_decoration()'s own guard shape and returns campaign_tally's
+           tally_segments() -- the same ordered segments the campaign table's public
+           Progress column renders (D-15: the two surfaces agree by construction).
+        {% endcomment %}
+        {% run_tally event as tally %}
+        {% if tally %}
+        <div class="small text-secondary" title="{{ tally.summary }}" aria-label="{{ tally.summary }}">
+          {{ tally.groups }} group{{ tally.groups|pluralize }} &middot; {{ tally.records }} record{{ tally.records|pluralize }}
+          {% for segment in tally.segments %}
+          &middot; {{ segment.marker }}
+          {% comment %}
+             WR-04-style guard (event_form.html's own window_start rule, above): a
+             not-yet-known unused figure must never render as a bare zero.
+          {% endcomment %}
+          {% if not segment.known %}
+          {{ segment.label }} not yet known
+          {% elif segment.is_estimate %}
+          &asymp;{{ segment.count }} {{ segment.label }} (estimate)
+          {% else %}
+          {{ segment.count }} {{ segment.label }}
+          {% endif %}
+          {% endfor %}
+        </div>
+        {% endif %}
+      </div>
+    </div>
+{% elif not event.telescope_label_meta.run and request.user.is_staff %}
+    {% comment %}
+       27-07 gap closure (27-UAT.md Test 9, T-27-21): `not run` is true both when
+       event.telescope_label_meta has no companion row at all and when the companion row
+       exists with run unset -- both are the same "not yet attributed" state
+       candidates_for_event() already treats as an orphan, so they are not special-cased
+       separately here. Staff-only via request.user.is_staff (server-derived from the
+       request, not client input, matching campaign_list.html's nav-banner gate
+       convention) -- an offered candidate run may not yet be publicly visible, so this
+       hint must never reach an anonymous or non-staff visitor.
+    {% endcomment %}
+    {% high_band_attribution_candidates event as attribution_candidates %}
+    {% if attribution_candidates %}
+    <div class="row">
+      <div class="col">
+        <label>Possible campaign run match</label>
+        {% for candidate in attribution_candidates %}
+        <div>
+          {{ candidate.run }}
+          <span class="badge text-bg-light border">{{ candidate.score }}</span>
+        </div>
+        {% endfor %}
+        <small>
+          <a href="{% url 'campaigns:attribution' %}?band=high" target="_blank">Confirm in the attribution queue ↗</a>
+        </small>
+      </div>
+    </div>
+    {% endif %}
+{% endif %}
